Feature: Validate and Convert delivery_dt in f_order Table

  Background:
    Given the table "purgo_playground.purgo_playground.f_order" is accessible

  Scenario: Validate if delivery_dt is in the correct Decimal(38,0) format
    Given the field "delivery_dt" in the table "f_order"
    When I retrieve the value of "delivery_dt"
    Then it should be a Decimal number with a precision of 38 and scale of 0
    And the format should be "yyyymmdd"

  Scenario: Convert valid delivery_dt from timestamp to Decimal(38,0)
    Given the field "delivery_dt" with value "2024-09-10"
    When I apply the conversion logic for timestamp to Decimal(38,0)
    Then the converted value should be "20240910"

  Scenario Outline: Handle invalid delivery_dt entries
    Given the field "delivery_dt" with value "<invalid_date>"
    When I check the format and datatype
    Then it should display an error message "<error_message>"

  Examples:
    | invalid_date     | error_message                        |
    | 2024/09/10       | "Invalid date format for delivery_dt" |
    | 10-09-2024       | "Invalid date format for delivery_dt" |
    | abcdefgh         | "Value is not a valid date"           |

  Scenario Outline: Check for 100% Decimal(38,0) compliance 
    Given a delivery_dt value "<test_value>" in the f_order table
    When I verify the compliance
    Then the result should be "<expected_result>"

  Examples:
    | test_value | expected_result |
    | 20240910   | true            |
    | 20240931   | false           |

  Scenario: Integration of converted data with target system
    Given a successfully converted "delivery_dt" value
    When I integrate it into the target system
    Then it should be usable in subsequent processes without errors
